/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    A rabbit's series is inserted into a series outside it, reached through a record made in the rabbit.

    A record is copied where it is stored, but what it holds is shared, so a store through it
    reaches the outer series (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, *Open*, closed 2026-11-25). */

Define rows as a series of series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define r as a record with (the t rows).
    Define xs as a series of number with (3, 2).
    Insert xs into the t of r.
Done.
State rows.
